<title>UK: Cathay International H1 profit dips.</title>
<headline>Cathay International H1 profit dips.</headline>
<text>
<p>LONDON, October 28 Reuter) - Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		0.13		   vs 0.07</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 nil		    vs nil</p>
<p> Pretax		     1.69		   vs 2.39</p>
<p> Turnover		   13.28		  vs 12.66</p>
<p> Operating profit	 2.34		   vs 2.94</p>
<p> Interest payable	 0.65		   vs 0.55</p>
<p> Tax			  0.53		   vs 1.05</p>
<p> Attributable	     0.40		   vs 0.23</p>
<p> Retained		   0.36		   vs 0.20</p>
<p>NOTE - Property investment and development company specialising in China, Cathay International Plc, said it plans to redeem preference shares when cash flow improves and it has built up distributable reserves.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
